<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Olynthiacs</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">349–348 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Olynthiacs are three political speeches delivered by the Athenian orator Demosthenes in 349–348 BCE. They urged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> to send effective help to Olynthus, the leading city of the Chalcidian League, which was under attack by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-macedon">Philip II of Macedon</a>. Athens sent only limited aid, and Philip captured and destroyed Olynthus in 348 BCE.</p></div>
